course: dictionary
lesson: 14738
title: Prominence: standing out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Prominence is a noun. It means being easy to see, or being well known and important. Look at the words around it for clues. «She rose to prominence as a singer.» The word rose tells you she became more famous over time, so prominence means being well known.
explain: «The story was given prominence on the front page.» The words front page are the clue. Newspapers put their most important stories there so everyone sees them. Here, prominence means being easy to see and noticed.
explain: A prominence can also be a real part of the land that sticks up, like a hill or a bump. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Does it still make sense? Then you have found the right meaning.
fact: Prominence means being well known or important, as in «rise to prominence».
fact: «Give prominence to» means to make something easy to see or notice.
fact: «Gain prominence» means to become more important or better known over time.
fact: A prominence can be a raised part of land, like a hill or a bump that sticks out.
fact: In space science, a solar prominence is a huge loop of glowing gas rising from the surface of the Sun.
exercise: «She rose to prominence as a singer.» What does prominence mean here? | Being hard to notice | A raised bump on the ground | *Being well known and important | A loud noise on stage
exercise: «The climbers rested on a rocky prominence above the valley.» What is a prominence in this sentence? | A group of climbers | A long, flat road | *A raised part of land that sticks up | A kind of rain
exercise: Which phrase means to make a story easy to see and notice? | prominence of the dark | rise to prominence | *give prominence to | solar panel
test: «The news was given prominence on the front page.» What does prominence mean? | Being a hill far away | *Being easy to see and noticed | Being quiet and hidden | Being very tired
test: «The singer gained prominence after her first song went viral.» What does gained prominence mean? | Sang in a small room | Lost her voice | *Became well known and important | Forgot the words
exam: Which meaning fits «a grassy prominence above the valley»? | Being well known and important | *A raised part of land | A kind of cloud | A loud sound from the valley
